{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses one-shot directed turns for side obstacles, uses brief backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use decision/action helper states so each non-perception state enables exactly one controllable event",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward with occasional random_walk and rare brief turns",
    "Route obstacle_front through dedicated recovery with brief backward escape before directed turning",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Allow full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck/last_resort state after repeated blocked outcomes"
  ],
